  "author": null,
  "summary": null,
  "thumbnail_url": null,
  "body": "<p>Discord has 5 <strong>status icons</strong> that are pretty simple representations of user status. They are as follows:</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Green = Online</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/article_attachments/1500010890901\" alt=\"online_status.png\"></p>\n<p>Yellow = Idle</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/article_attachments/1500010890801\" alt=\"idle_status.png\"></p>\n<p>Red = Do Not Disturb</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/article_attachments/1500010890821\" alt=\"do_not_disturb_status.png\"></p>\n<p>Purple = Streaming</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/article_attachments/1500010890921\" alt=\"streaming_status.png\"></p>\n<p>Gray = Invisible/Offline</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://support.discord.com/hc/article_attachments/1500010890861\" alt=\"invisible_status.png\"></p>\n<p>  </p>\n<p>Keep in mind that you only get put into idle status when you've been away from your device for a while- similar to being moved to an AFK (away from keyboard) voice channel. And while Offline doesn't have a dot, you'll see the user's name and avatar grayed out pretty thoroughly.</p>",
